  "hh_ethnologue_comment": {
    "comment": "Mutsun and Rumsen are joined in a Southern Ohlone [css] language in E16/E17/E18/E19/E20/E21/E22/E23/E24/E25/E26/E27/E28/E29. The two are arguably distinct languages as they share only 61% of basic vocabulary and were sociopolitically separate (**hh:hv:Callaghan:Utian-Swadesh**:233, **hh:hvb:Golla:California**:165-166, **hh:hvw:Callaghan:Utian**:14-18). See also: Mutsun [css].",
